# Telescope (GAME-TELESCOPE): the eight planets, one sentence per reading level.
telescope-title = Stars and planets
telescope-close = Close telescope
telescope-hint = Tap a planet!
telescope-kind-rocky = Rocky planet
telescope-kind-gas = Gas giant
telescope-kind-ice = Ice giant

telescope-mercury-name = Mercury
telescope-mercury-kiga = Mercury is tiny.
telescope-mercury-klasse1 = Mercury is the smallest planet. It is nearest the Sun.
telescope-mercury-klasse2 = Mercury is the smallest planet and closest to the Sun. A year there lasts only 88 days.
telescope-mercury-klasse3 = Mercury is the smallest planet, about 4,900 kilometres across, and the closest to the Sun. By day it is scorching hot, at night icy cold.

telescope-venus-name = Venus
telescope-venus-kiga = Venus is very hot.
telescope-venus-klasse1 = Venus is very hot. It has thick clouds.
telescope-venus-klasse2 = Venus is wrapped in thick clouds and is the hottest planet. In the sky it shines as a bright evening star.
telescope-venus-klasse3 = Venus is wrapped in a thick blanket of clouds and, at about 460 degrees, is the hottest planet. From Earth you can see it as a bright morning or evening star.

telescope-earth-name = Earth
telescope-earth-kiga = Earth is our home.
telescope-earth-klasse1 = Earth is our home. It has much water.
telescope-earth-klasse2 = Earth is the only planet where we know there is life. From space it looks blue because there is so much water.
telescope-earth-klasse3 = Earth is the third planet and the only one where we know there is life. More than two thirds of its surface are covered with water.

telescope-mars-name = Mars
telescope-mars-kiga = Mars is red.
telescope-mars-klasse1 = Mars is red. Its dust is rusty.
telescope-mars-klasse2 = Mars is also called the red planet. It is red because its dust is rusty.
telescope-mars-klasse3 = Mars is a rocky planet called the red planet, because its dust contains iron that rusts. It has two small moons.

telescope-jupiter-name = Jupiter
telescope-jupiter-kiga = Jupiter is huge.
telescope-jupiter-klasse1 = Jupiter is the biggest planet. It has a storm.
telescope-jupiter-klasse2 = Jupiter is the biggest planet. Its Great Red Spot is a giant storm.
telescope-jupiter-klasse3 = Jupiter is a gas giant and the biggest planet: more than 1,000 Earths would fit inside. Its Great Red Spot is a storm that has been raging for hundreds of years.

telescope-saturn-name = Saturn
telescope-saturn-kiga = Saturn has a ring.
telescope-saturn-klasse1 = Saturn has a ring. The ring is ice.
telescope-saturn-klasse2 = Saturn is a gas giant. You recognise it by its ring, which is made of countless pieces of ice and rock.
telescope-saturn-klasse3 = Saturn is a gas giant and easy to recognise by its ring. The ring is made of countless chunks of ice and rock, from tiny grains to pieces as big as a house.

telescope-uranus-name = Uranus
telescope-uranus-kiga = Uranus is light blue.
telescope-uranus-klasse1 = Uranus is light blue. It lies on its side.
telescope-uranus-klasse2 = Uranus is an ice giant and looks light blue. It rolls around the Sun lying on its side.
telescope-uranus-klasse3 = Uranus is an ice giant and glows light blue-green. Its axis is tilted so far that it rolls around the Sun on its side.

telescope-neptune-name = Neptune
telescope-neptune-kiga = Neptune is deep blue.
telescope-neptune-klasse1 = Neptune is deep blue. It is farthest away.
telescope-neptune-klasse2 = Neptune is an ice giant and the farthest planet. It is deep blue and has very strong winds.
telescope-neptune-klasse3 = Neptune is an ice giant and the planet farthest from the Sun. It is deep blue, and the fastest winds of the solar system blow there.
